                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_99\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit (\"fixed /help bug\") removes an entire caching/reload mechanism for command help text: it deletes `CommandParser.reload()`, `AbstractCommand.reloadText()` (and its overrides in `InvalidCommand`, `OnlinePlayerArgCommand`, `PlayerArgCommand`), the mutable `helpText` field, and the call to `commandParser.reload()` in `Server.java`. In its place, the fix computes the help text lazily on every call to `getHelpText()` using a new immutable `help` field plus `t(commandCode)` (the translation lookup), instead of caching a pre-built, pre-translated string.\n\nTracing this mechanism back through the candidates, `candidate_99` is exactly where it was introduced. That commit:\n- Adds `simpleserver.lang.Translations` (`t`) as the localization system and changes `AbstractCommand`'s constructor to build and cache `helpText` at construction time using `t.get(commandCode)` (`helpText = name + \"\u00a7f : \" + t.get(commandCode);`).\n- Adds `CommandParser.reload()`, which iterates over all server/player commands and calls `((AbstractCommand) command).reloadText()`.\n- Adds `AbstractCommand.reloadText()` (and overrides in `InvalidCommand`, `OnlinePlayerArgCommand`, `PlayerArgCommand`) to recompute the cached `helpText` after the fact.\n- Wires `commandParser.reload()` into `Server.java`'s `reload()` method, right after `t.setLanguage(...)`, so that command help text is (supposedly) refreshed once the correct language is loaded.\n\nThis design is fundamentally the root cause of the `/help` bug: commands are constructed (and their help text cached) via `CommandParser`'s `loadCommands()` before the server's language/translation resource has necessarily been loaded/reloaded in every code path, and the `reload()`/`reloadText()` synchronization mechanism is fragile \u2014 any place where `reload()` isn't invoked, or is invoked in the wrong order relative to language loading, leaves `/help` displaying stale, untranslated, or incorrect text. The eventual fix eliminates the caching entirely (computing the text on demand in `getHelpText()`), which only makes sense as a fix if this caching/reload scheme (introduced in candidate_99) was the actual source of the bug. No earlier candidate contains any `helpText`/`reloadText`/translation caching logic that matches what the fix removes \u2014 `candidate_55` (and subsequent commits before 99) has help text cached in a single `final` field with no reload path at all, so there is no stale-cache bug possible there. Later candidates (108, 110, 117, 126, 131) only extend or reuse this same `reloadText`/`helpText` pattern established in candidate_99, without introducing the caching/reload architecture itself.\n"
                }
              }
            ]
